## 3. 5-year forecast: to 2030

Extending the time to 5 years will multiply the uncertainty.

| Scenario | Revenue compound growth rate | Net profit margin assumption | 2030 revenue | 2030 net profit |
|------|------------|-----------|-----------|-------------|
| Optimistic | 25% | 28% | ~112 billion | ~31.4 billion |
| Neutral | 15% | 23% | ~74.7 billion | ~17.2 billion |
| Pessimistic | 5% | 18% | ~47.4 billion | ~8.5 billion |

Five-year forecasts are more like drawing targets. But its value lies in forcing you to think clearly about a question: **What exactly is Bubble Mart? **

If it is a **consumer products company**, it will be very difficult for the five-year compound growth rate to exceed 15%. The fate of consumer goods is saturated channels, aging categories, and a red ocean of competition.

If it is an **IP platform** - similar to Disney and Nintendo with IP assets that can be repeatedly monetized - then the growth ceiling depends on the depth of the IP portfolio and the diversity of monetization forms. Movies, games, theme parks, each of them is a multiplier effect.

Which category you put it into directly determines how you value it.

