## 5. Final judgment: no conclusion, only standards

I'm not going to tell you "should you buy" or "shouldn't buy". This conclusion makes no sense - the answer is completely different for people with different amounts of funds, different holding periods, and different risk preferences.

Three judgment criteria, you can choose the right one by yourself:

**Criterion 1: Do you think Bubble Mart is an "IP platform" or a "hot consumer product"? **

If you believe that it is an IP platform - it has the organizational ability to continuously produce super IP, and overseas channels are long-term assets - then a price-to-earnings ratio of 12 to 15 times is obviously undervalued. The valuation of IP platform companies in the growth stage is usually 25 to 35 times.

If you think that it is essentially a consumer goods company driven by explosive products, and its current growth rate is mainly supported by a super cycle of LABUBU - then the current price is only reasonable, not cheap.

**Criterion 2: How much volatility can you tolerate? **

The stock of Bubble Mart fell 90% in 2022, rose 10 times in 2024, and fell 30% in two days in March 2026. If it falls by 40% after buying it, you will not be able to sleep. No matter how good the fundamentals are, it is not suitable.

**Standard 3: Do you have your own judgment on the variable "IP life cycle"? **

How long can LABUBU remain popular? When will the next super IP be released? No one can answer this question, including Wang Ning himself. It is essentially a probabilistic question, not an analytical question.

